            <ArticleTitle>[Surgical treatment of high occlusion of the abdominal aorta associated with lesions of coronary, renal and visceral arteries].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>39-43</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The results of surgical treatment of 158 patients with high occlusion of the abdominal aorta associated with lesion of the coronary, renal and visceral arteries are presented. The technique of aorto-femoral shunting from the descending aorta with isolated plasty of its branches in patients with concomitant severe coronary disease, permitting to reduce the incidence of complications and lethality, is suggested.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
